  ⧗:C̵,F,c,nc,m1 ⧗:fi
  ⍿⁰ ○ ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ⌁ ⧖:C,FF,cc,ncc,mm ⧗:C̵,FF,cc ‹pvfact› ⧖:C,F2 ⧗:C̵,F2,ncc ‹pvfact› ⦄ ⦃
  △ ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ⧖:C,FF,cc,ncc,mm ⧗:C̵,cc,mm △ ‹afcomb› ⧖:C,g ⧗:C̵,FF,g ‹pvfact› ⦄
    ⦃ ⧖:C,FF,cc,ncc,mm ⧗:C̵,ncc,mm △ ‹afcomb› ⧖:C,g ⧗:C̵,FF,g ‹pvfact› ⦄ ⁼ ⦄ ⁼
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ⟩ ‹pvfacts› ⸫

⍝ ---- the measure and what it must do

⍝ ‹pvmeasure› C vals: the vow's measure on vals (−1 unless it is one affine value)
⦃
  ⧖:C,vals
  ⧗:C̵ #10# ‹a2› ⧖:C,vw
  ⧗:C̵ ‹lnew0› ⧖:C,st
  ⧗:C̵,vals,st #-1# ○ ‹pvmk› ⧖:C,p
  ⧗:C̵ ⧗:vw #3# ⊞ ⧗:p ‹pvblockin› ⧖:C,L
  ⧗:C̵,L ‹llen› ⧖:C,n
  ⧗:C̵,L ⧗:n △ ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ○ ‹lget› ‹pvS› ⧖:C,S ⧗:C̵,S ‹llen› ⧖:C,ns ⧗:C̵,S ⧗:ns △ ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ○ ‹lget› ⦄ ⦃ ⌁ #-1# ⦄ ⁼ ⦄ ⦃ ⌁ #-1# ⦄ ⁼ ⧖:C,m
  ⧗:C̵,m ⧗:m #-1# ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ⦄ ⦃ ⧖:C,mm ⧗:C̵,mm ‹aftag› ⧖:C,t ⧗:C̵ ⧗:mm #-1# ⧗:t ○ ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ⌁ ⦄ ⦃ ⧖ ⌁ ⧗⁰ ⦄ ⁼ ⦄ ⁼
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ⟩ ‹pvmeasure› ⸫
⍝ ‹pvoblig› C vals F vg: on a path with facts F the vow's measure goes from slot 11's to that
⍝ of vals; it must be at least 0 and at least 1 lower (perjury only on a path that is not vague)
⦃
  ⧖:C,vals,F,vg
  ⧗:C̵,vals ‹pvmeasure› ⧖:C,m
  ⧗:C̵ #11# ‹a2› ⧖:C,m0
  ⧗:C̵,m,m0,F,vg ⧗:m #-1# ᛖ ⧗:m0 #-1# ᛖ ⋏ ⋔ ⦃ ⌁ ⌁ ⌁ ⌁ ‹pvstop› ⌁ ⦄ ⦃ ‹pvoblig1› ⦄ ⁼
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧⟩ ‹pvoblig› ⸫
⦃
  ⧖:C,m,m0,F,vg
  ⧗:C̵,m,F ‹afgeq› ⧖:C,pos
  ⧗:C̵,m0,m #-1# ‹afcomb› ⧖:C,dd ⧗:C̵ ○ #-1# ‹afnew› ⧖:C,one ⧗:C̵,dd,one △ ‹afcomb› ⧖:C,dec
  ⧗:C̵,dec,F ‹afgeq› ⧖:C,down
  ⍝ m − m0 a constant ≥ 0 on a path that can be taken: the vow is false
  ⧗:C̵,m,m0 #-1# ‹afcomb› ⧖:C,up
  ⧗:C̵,up,F ‹afgeq› ⧖:C,rises ⧗:C̵,up ‹afisconst› ⧖:C,upc ⧗:C̵,F ‹pvfeasible› ⧖:C,feas
  ⧗:C̵ #8# ‹a2› ⧖:C,s
  ⧗:s ⧗:pos ⧗:down ⋎ ⋔ ⦃ ⦄ ⦃ △ ‹max› ⦄ ⁼ ⧗:rises ⧗:upc ⋎ ⧗:feas ⋎ ⧗:vg ○ ᛖ ⋎ ⋔ ⦃ ⌁ #2# ⦄ ∅ ⁼ ⧖:s2
  ⧗:C̵ #8# ⧗:s2 ‹a2w›
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧⟩ ‹pvoblig1› ⸫

⍝ ‹pvsyms› C ts: a symbol for each ℤ of the types ts, unknown for the rest
⦃
  ⧖:C,ts
  ⧗:C̵ ‹lnew0› ⧖:C,S
  ⧗:C̵,ts ‹llen› ⧖:C,n
  ⧗:C̵,ts,S ○ ⧗:n
  ⥀ ⦃
    ⧖:C,ts,S,j,n
    ⧗:C̵,ts,S,j,n ⧗:j ⧗:n ≶ ⋔ ⦃ ⦶ ⦄ ⁼
      ⦃ ⧖:C,ts,S,j,n ⧗:C̵,ts,j ‹lget› ⧖:C,t ⧗:C̵,t #11# ‹tis› ⧖:C,isz
        ⧗:C̵,j ⧗:isz ⋔ ⦃ ‹afvar› ⦄ ⦃ ⌁ ‹afunk› ⦄ ⁼ ⧖:C,v ⧗:C̵,S,v ‹lpush› ⧖:C,S2
        ⧗:C̵,ts,S2 ⧗:j △ ⊞ ⧗:n ⊕ ⦄
  ⦄
  ⧖:C,ts,S,j,n ⧗:C̵,S
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ⟩ ‹pvsyms› ⸫
⍝ ‹pvstart› C k name vw es: the prover's state for one vow
⦃
  ⧖:C,k,name,vw,es
  ⧗:C̵ #7# ⧗:k ‹a2w› #8# ○ ‹a2w› #9# ⧗:name ‹a2w› #10# ⧗:vw ‹a2w› #11# #-1# ‹a2w› #12# ○ ‹a2w› #13# ⧗:es ‹a2w›
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧⟩ ‹pvstart› ⸫
⍝ ‹pvend› C tok: the status as ‹vprove› reports it (bit 1 proven); perjury stops here
⦃
  ⧖:C,tok
  ⧗:C̵ #8# ‹a2› ⧖:C,s
  ⧗:C̵ ⧗:s #2# ᛖ ‹not› ⧗:tok #35# ‹cfailunless›
  ○ ⧗:s ○ ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ⌁ △ ⦄ ∅ ⁼
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ⟩ ‹pvend› ⸫

⍝ ‹vprove› C pv op S strand: the vow pv of ⥀ op, entered with stack S in a block with moments
⍝ strand. Results: bit 1 proven, bit 2 the ⥀ never exits with ⊖.
⦃
  ⧖:C,pv,op,S,strand
  ⧗:C̵,S ‹llen› ⧖:C,k
  ⧗:C̵,k #-1# ⧗:pv,strand ‹pvstart› ⧖:C
  ⧗:C̵,S ‹ltypes› ⧖:C,ts ⧗:C̵,ts ‹pvsyms› ⧖:C,HS
  ⧗:C̵,HS ‹pvmeasure› ⧖:C,mh ⧗:C̵ #11# ⧗:mh ‹a2w› ⧖:C
  ⧗:C̵ ⧗:mh #-1# ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ‹pvstop› ⌁ ⦄ ∅ ⁼ ⧖:C
  ⧗:C̵ ‹lnew0› ⧖:C,st0
  ⧗:C̵,HS,st0 #-1# ○ ‹pvmk› ‹l1› ⧖:C,L0
  ⧗:C̵ ⧗:op #3# ⊞ ‹brange› ⧖:C,from,to
  ⧗:C̵,from,to,L0 ‹pvblock› ⧖:C,L
  ⧗:C̵,L ‹llen› ⧖:C,n
  ⧗:C̵,L ○ ⧗:n ⦶
  ⥀ ⦃
    ⧖:C,L,j,n,nofail
    ⧗:C̵,L,j,n,nofail ⧗:j ⧗:n ≶ ⋔ ⦃ ⦶ ⦄ ⁼
      ⦃ ⧖:C,L,j,n,nofail ⧗:C̵,L,j ‹lget› ‹pvloopend› ⧖:C,nf ⧗:C̵,L ⧗:j △ ⊞ ⧗:n ⧗:nofail ⧗:nf ⋎ ⊕ ⦄
  ⦄
  ⧖:C,L,j,n,nofail
  ⧗:C̵,pv ‹ndt› ⧖:C,tok
  ⧗:C̵,tok ‹pvend› ⧖:C,r
  ⧗:C̵ #12# ‹a2› ⧖:C,fl
  ⧗:C̵ ⧗:r ⧗:nofail ⧗:fl ○ ᛖ ⋎ ⋔ ⦃ #2# ⋓ ⦄ ∅ ⁼
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ⟩ ‹vprove› ⸫
⍝ ‹pvloopend› C p: a path round the body; if its trit can be ⊕ the measure must fall. Gives
⍝ whether it never leaves with ⊖.
⦃
  ⧖:C,p
  ⧗:C̵,p ‹pvS› ⧖:C,S ⧗:C̵,p ‹pvF› ⧖:C,F ⧗:C̵,p ‹pvv› ⧖:C,v
  ⧗:C̵,S ‹llen› ⧖:C,n
  ⧗:C̵,S ⧗:n △ ⊟ ‹lget› ⧖:C,t
  ⧗:C̵,S ○ ⧗:n △ ⊟ ‹lslice› ⧖:C,BS
  ⍝ the trit is the sign of g: known (tc), or linear (facts), or unknown
  ⧗:C̵,t ‹aftag› ⧖:C,tt
  ⧗:C̵,t ⧗:tt △ ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ‹afg› ⦄ ⦃ ⌁ ‹afunk› ⦄ ⁼ ⧖:C,g
  ⧗:C̵,g ‹afisconst› ⧖:C,tc ⧗:C̵,g ‹afc› ⧖:C,tv
  ⧗:tt △ ᛖ ⧖:istrit
  ⧗:istrit ⧗:tc ⋎ ⧖:known ⧗:istrit ⧗:tc ‹not› ⋎ ⧖:lin
  ⧗:C̵ ○ #-1# ‹afnew› ⧖:C,m1 ⧗:C̵,g,m1 △ ‹afcomb› ⧖:C,g1
  ⧗:C̵,F,g1 ‹pvfact› ⧖:C,Fc
  ⧗:Fc ⧗:F ⧗:lin ⋔ ⦃ ⌁ ⦄ ⦃ ⧖ ⌁ ⧗⁰ ⦄ ⁼ ⧖:Fgo
  ○ ⧗:v △ ᛖ ⧗:known ⧗:lin ⋏ ‹not› ⋏ ⋔ ⦃ ⌁ △ ⦄ ∅ ⁼ ⧖:vg
  ⍝ can it go round?
  ⧗:known ‹not› ⧗:tv ○ ≶ ⋔ ⦃ ⊕ ⦄ ⦃ ⦶ ⦄ ⦃ ⊕ ⦄ ⋏ ⧖:goes
  ⧗:C̵,BS,Fgo,vg ⧗:goes ⋔ ⦃ ‹pvoblig› ⦄ ⦃ ⌁ ⌁ ⌁ ⦄ ⁼ ⧖:C
  ⍝ can it leave with ⊖? not when the trit is known ≥ 0 or g ≥ 0 follows
  ⧗:C̵,g,F ‹afgeq› ⧖:C,gpos
  ⧗:C̵ ⧗:known ⧗:tv ○ ≶ ⋔ ⦃ ⦶ ⦄ ⦃ ⦶ ⦄ ⦃ ⊕ ⦄ ⋎ ⧗:lin ⧗:gpos ⋎ ⋏
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ŧ⟩ ‹pvloopend› ⸫

⍝ ‹vprovefn› C f vw from to: the vow vw of function f, whose body is from … to−1
⦃
  ⧖:C,f,vw,from,to
  ⧗:C̵,f △ ‹vf› ⧖:C,ins ⧗:C̵,ins ‹llen› ⧖:C,k
  ⧗:C̵,f #24# ‹vf› ⧖:C,name
  ⧗:C̵ ‹lnew0› ⧖:C,es
  ⧗:C̵,k,name,vw,es ‹pvstart› ⧖:C
  ⧗:C̵,ins ‹pvsyms› ⧖:C,HS
  ⧗:C̵,HS ‹pvmeasure› ⧖:C,mh ⧗:C̵ #11# ⧗:mh ‹a2w› ⧖:C
  ⧗:C̵ ⧗:mh #-1# ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ‹pvstop› ⌁ ⦄ ∅ ⁼ ⧖:C
  ⧗:C̵ ‹lnew0› ⧖:C,st0
  ⧗:C̵,HS,st0 #-1# ○ ‹pvmk› ‹l1› ⧖:C,L0
  ⧗:C̵,from,to,L0 ‹pvblock› ⌁ ⧖:C
  ⧗:C̵,vw ‹ndt› ‹pvend›
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ⟩ ‹vprovefn› ⸫
